; facetec-api default scan acceptance rules — SPOCP advanced format
; Each rule must be on a single line. Atoms are unquoted.
;
; Numeric thresholds are encoded as SPOCP range predicates (* range numeric ...).
; Liveness scores are 3-digit zero-padded integers (000-100).
; Face match levels are 2-digit zero-padded integers (00-10).
;
; Field order: liveness-score, face-match-level, doc-type, mrz-verified,
;              nfc-verified, barcode-verified, chip-trusted
; Rules may stop at any field — trailing query fields beyond the rule are ignored.
;
; chip-trusted is true only when facetec-api itself verified the eMRTD chip
; (SOD signature + data-group hashes + DG1/MRZ cross-check) AND the go-trust PDP
; says the document signer chains to a reviewed CSCA for the issuing state.
; It is independent of nfc-verified, which is FaceTec's own chip authentication
; (clone detection via Active/Chip Authentication plus FaceTec's signature
; verification, nfcAuthenticationStatusEnumInt 4).
; Positional matching means a rule that constrains chip-trusted must also list
; the fields before it; (* set true false) matches either value.
;
; Only nfcAuthenticationStatusEnumInt 4 (AUTHENTICATED) is accepted, for every
; document type; /process-request refuses every other status in code before
; these rules run. In particular a passport whose chip has no Active/Chip
; Authentication (status 1) is refused by design.
;
; Default thresholds: liveness >= 80, face-match >= 06.
; To tighten or relax thresholds per deployment, edit these rules directly.

; Note that Facetec itself has a configuration for minimum 3D:2D match level that will be used 
; to trigger a warning about "manual review" in the device SDK. This is not covered by these rules.

; Every rule requires an authenticated NFC chip (nfc-verified true): FaceTec
; status 4, i.e. clone detection (AA/CA) and FaceTec's signature verification
; succeeded. A document without one is never accepted, whatever else it
; scores (#65). facetec-api also refuses such scans outright before
; evaluating these rules; the requirement is repeated here so that a rule
; edited without it cannot silently re-admit chipless documents.
; Passports additionally require (chip-trusted true): facetec-api's own passive
; authentication succeeded AND the go-trust PDP says the document signer chains
; to our reviewed CSCA list. Both are required: status 4 proves the chip is not
; a clone, chip-trusted proves the data was signed by a state we trust.
; Positional matching: a rule constraining chip-trusted must list every field
; before it, hence the (barcode-verified (* set true false)) placeholder.
; "(mrz-verified)" with no value accepts either outcome.

; Accept e-passports: MRZ verified, chip authenticated AND trusted
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type passport) (mrz-verified true) (nfc-verified true) (barcode-verified (* set true false)) (chip-trusted true))
; Accept national ID cards with an authenticated NFC chip
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type id_card) (mrz-verified) (nfc-verified true))
; Accept driving licences with an authenticated NFC chip
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type dl) (mrz-verified) (nfc-verified true))

; --- Operator review rules (ETSI 119 461 §4.5 escalation) ---
; NOTE: These rules use the "facetec-scan-review" head atom. The policy engine
; must query both "facetec-scan" (for accept/reject) and "facetec-scan-review"
; (for escalation) to enable the operator review path.
; Escalate borderline passports: liveness >= 60 AND face-match >= 4
; (entries that also satisfy the accept rules above will match accept first)
; A passport whose chip is not trusted must not be escalated for acceptance.
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type passport) (mrz-verified true) (nfc-verified true) (barcode-verified (* set true false)) (chip-trusted true))
; Escalate borderline ID cards
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type id_card) (mrz-verified) (nfc-verified true))
; Escalate borderline driving licences
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type dl) (mrz-verified) (nfc-verified true))
